Now I have a key insight. In the `split_ctoken` function (L81-103 in ctoken_table.move):

When the balance reaches 0 (L90):
```
if (in_bag_balance.value() == 0) {
    self.coin_types.remove<TypeName, CoinType>();
    // ...
    self.ctoken_values.remove(ctoken_type);
}
```

This means when the ctoken balance reaches 0 after withdrawal, the type is REMOVED from the ctoken table. So `supported_coin_types()` (which is `deposit_types()` in the obligation) would no longer include this coin type.


This is important because in `collaterals_usd_non_liquidation`, the function iterates through `deposit_types()` and calculates the USD value for each type—after a full withdrawal, that type simply won't appear in the list anymore, so its contribution correctly becomes 0. Let me check how `ctoken_amount_by_coin` works in the obligation module to confirm the full picture.

